Thanks Andy,

To be more precise the data I have is for shorebirds during the non breeding season, with counts taken while the birds are roosting. There are therefore either 0 or hundreds of birds visible during a count. The total population across the sites does not vary much,
though it does appear to be declining; 20 years ago you would get counts
 of 6000 birds, now, no larger than 2000.

Would it be worthwhile aggregating some of the sites together (where we know the birds are either at one roost or the other) to reduce some of the variation in the data? The problem of the high K would remain though because the counts are still big. Is there not a good way to scale/transform the data so that ranef() can deal with it?

Would it be worthwhile even doing it in JAGS?

Thanks for the help,
Kaz

